# Styling & Theming

## Color System
All colors are defined in `src/constants/Colors.ts` with `light` and `dark` variants:
- `text`, `textSecondary` — Primary and secondary text
- `background`, `backgroundSecondary` — Main and card/section backgrounds
- `tint` — Accent/brand color
- `border`, `icon`, `danger`, `success` — Semantic colors

## Using Colors in Components
```typescript
import { useThemeColor } from "../hooks/useThemeColor";

function MyComponent() {
  const colors = useThemeColor();
  return <View style={{ backgroundColor: colors.background }} />;
}
```

Or use themed wrappers: `ThemedView`, `ThemedText`, `Card`, `Button`.

## Layout Constants
Use `src/constants/Layout.ts` for consistent spacing:
- `Layout.spacing.xs` (4) through `Layout.spacing.xxl` (48)
- `Layout.borderRadius.sm` (6) through `Layout.borderRadius.full` (9999)
- `Layout.fontSize.xs` (12) through `Layout.fontSize.title` (34)

## Rules
- Always use `StyleSheet.create()` — never inline style objects
- Use `StyleSheet.hairlineWidth` for thin borders
- Gap property is supported in RN 0.83+
